From: Ilija Tovilo <ilija.tovilo@me.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 16:49:38 +0200
Subject: Fix SQL injection in ext-pgsql via E'...' backslash breakout

php_pgsql_add_quotes() quotes the string with E'...', but PQescapeStringConn()
does not escape \ unless standard_conforming_strings is off.
PQescapeStringConn() is meant to be used with '', so do that instead.

Fixes GHSA-7qpv-r5mr-78m4

(cherry picked from commit ab048bd83b578119cf81b456526d50498421d617)
(cherry picked from commit eb0de306e0569f8b50065a42f13dd3e2b3729532)
(cherry picked from commit 531196af8ccc43c26ca97aef27b0816e8b4e2f60)
(cherry picked from commit 6a80d9d36a5ea210ea6cc411864c08c71f7417ec)
(cherry picked from commit 72c3531150e451cdfca49b16879257c6de6e2880)
(cherry picked from commit a33d0c050d938889930c6a6a403d0a563c968301)
(cherry picked from commit 19f3b5bca1b6669c8c4b7f8e4c2a0f13b908ccfd)
(cherry picked from commit f4b24bc502fd9f0f9cbdb8d0df69bc8f3e84bfdf)

debian-php-backports: ported to PHP 5.4.45 (php5 5.4.45-0+deb7u30): the code
change is the same: php_pgsql_add_quotes() no longer adds the E prefix. The
second pgsql.c hunk only removes a comment that 5.4 does not have, so it is
dropped. Tests: 10pg_convert_json_array.phpt and bug68638.phpt are not in 5.4
and are dropped; the expected E'...' lines in 12pg_insert_9.phpt and
14pg_update_9.phpt (other context in 5.4) are changed the same way; in
GHSA-7qpv-r5mr-78m4.phpt the PGSQL_DML_ESCAPE part is removed (5.4 has no
PGSQL_DML_ESCAPE).
